  <bpmn:process id="L4_02_P_SPON_PROCESS" name="Sponsor" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation textFormat="text/plain">SCP-03: 16 activities (target 5-15) - user decision 06 Nov 2026 to merge identification channels; 26 nodes, within 31.
Sponsor-to-investigator flows M1 and M2 end on the Investigator/institution pool: a target node would form a cycle with the investigator's reports (layout constraint), and the investigator's review of communicated deviations is modelled in L4-04. Investigator reports enter the sponsor where they are reviewed: deviation report and premature unblinding explanation in centralised data review A1 (FDA-PD24 SIII.B.2: sponsors receive deviation information mainly through monitoring), system incident and suspected serious breach reports in the sponsor review A11, which takes the detection decision.
Legal monitoring duties (EU CTR Art. 48, 21 CFR 312.50/312.56(a)) sit on the timer start event because they cover both channels.
A10 'Document monitoring report' follows the OR join G2 (V1 round 1): a monitoring report follows site and/or centralised monitoring activities (E6R3 GL:Monitoring Report, REQ-059), so both channels feed the sponsor review A11; Monitor lane because REQ-059 places the report on the monitor.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="L4_02_P_SPON_LANESET">
      <bpmn:lane id="L4_02_L_SPON" name="Sponsor">
        <bpmn:documentation textFormat="text/plain">Sources: E6R3 GL:Sponsor (p. printed 90 / PDF 98); EUCTR Art. 2(2)(14) (p. OJ L 158/12); 21CFR312 21CFR312.50 (p. n/a - eCFR web text without pagination)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:extensionElements>
          <ipd:trace>
            <ipd:source key="E6R3" loc="GL:Sponsor" page="printed 90 / PDF 98"/>
            <ipd:source key="EUCTR" loc="Art. 2(2)(14)" page="OJ L 158/12"/>
            <ipd:source key="21CFR312" loc="21CFR312.50" page="n/a - eCFR web text without pagination"/>
          </ipd:trace>
        </bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>L4_02_S1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>L4_02_G1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>L4_02_A1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>L4_02_A2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>L4_02_A3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>L4_02_A4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>L4_02_A5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>L4_02_G2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>L4_02_A11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>L4_02_G3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>L4_02_A12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>L4_02_E1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>L4_02_E2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="L4_02_L_MON" name="Monitor">
        <bpmn:documentation textFormat="text/plain">Sources: E6R3 A1-3.11.4.5.1(a) (p. printed 32 / PDF 40); E6R3 A1-3.11.4.4 (p. printed 32 / PDF 40)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:extensionElements>
          <ipd:trace>
            <ipd:source key="E6R3" loc="A1-3.11.4.5.1(a)" page="printed 32 / PDF 40"/>
            <ipd:source key="E6R3" loc="A1-3.11.4.4" page="printed 32 / PDF 40"/>
          </ipd:trace>
        </bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>L4_02_A6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>L4_02_A7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>L4_02_A8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>L4_02_A9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>L4_02_A10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="L4_02_S1" name="Monitoring activity scheduled">
      <bpmn:documentation textFormat="text/plain">Sources: EUCTR Art. 48 (p. OJ L 158/39); 21CFR312 21CFR312.50 (p. n/a - eCFR web text without pagination); 21CFR312 21CFR312.56(a) (p. n/a - eCFR web text without pagination)
Requirements: REQ-048, REQ-049
Binding: binding-law
Jurisdiction: EU, US
Deadline: continuous
Party: sponsor</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <ipd:trace binding="binding-law" jurisdiction="EU US" deadline="continuous" party="sponsor">
          <ipd:source key="EUCTR" loc="Art. 48" page="OJ L 158/39"/>
          <ipd:source key="21CFR312" loc="21CFR312.50" page="n/a - eCFR web text without pagination"/>
          <ipd:source key="21CFR312" loc="21CFR312.56(a)" page="n/a - eCFR web text without pagination"/>
          <ipd:req id="REQ-048"/>
          <ipd:req id="REQ-049"/>
        </ipd:trace>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:outgoing>L4_02_F1</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:timerEventDefinition/>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:inclusiveGateway id="L4_02_G1" name="Which monitoring channels are due?" gatewayDirection="Diverging">
      <bpmn:documentation textFormat="text/plain">Justification: Centralised monitoring can complement and reduce site monitoring or be used on its own (E6R3 A1-3.11.4.2(b)) and site visit frequency follows the risks (A1-3.11.4.1(a)), so one or both channels run in a cycle (FLW-07, DEC-02). Both outgoing flows are conditional and there is no default flow: the trigger 'Monitoring activity scheduled' guarantees at least one channel, and a default flow would wrongly suppress centralised review whenever a site visit is due (an OR default flow runs only when no other condition holds). XOR rejected: the channels are not exclusive.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>L4_02_F1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>L4_02_F2</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>L4_02_F3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:inclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:task id="L4_02_A1" name="Review trial data for protocol deviations">
      <bpmn:documentation textFormat="text/plain">Sources: E6R3 A1-3.11.4.5.4(b)(ii) (p. printed 34 / PDF 42); E6R3 A1-3.11.4.2(a) (p. printed 31 / PDF 39); E6R3 A1-3.11.4.2(b) (p. printed 31 / PDF 39); E8R1 S6.1.3 (p. printed 18); E8R1 S3.3.2 (p. printed 6); E6R3 A1-3.11.3 (p. printed 30 / PDF 38); E6R3 A1-3.16.1(b) (p. printed 39 / PDF 47); E6R3 A2-3.8 (p. printed 62 / PDF 70); E6R3 A1-3.11.4.5.4(c) (p. printed 34 / PDF 42); FDA-RBM13 SIII.B (p. printed 8); FDA-PD24 SIII.B.2 (p. printed 6; lines 227-228; printed 9; lines 314-317); TCB-PD-TIRS SIdentify-and-Collect (p. journal pp. 733-742 (section page not confirmed; PMC HTML read))
Requirements: REQ-037, REQ-036, REQ-035, REQ-038, REQ-040, REQ-041
Binding: binding-ICH
Jurisdiction: ICH, US
Deadline: timely (REQ-036); early (REQ-041)
Record: centralised monitoring report; deviation listings; oversight / monitoring plan
Party: sponsor; CRAs; site monitors and centralized monitoring
Draft: DRAFT guidance
Verify: [verify] gerund item under A1-3.11.4.5; actor not named (R1 C7); [verify binding] EU/US adoption of E8R1 not checked by the research stems (C-06); [verify] R1-089 is Annex 2: effective in the EU from 15 Jan 2027; FDA Annex 2 guidance still draft (C-06); [verify] basis is draft guidance only - shown as DRAFT, never a binding step</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <ipd:trace binding="binding-ICH" jurisdiction="ICH US" deadline="timely (REQ-036); early (REQ-041)" draft="true" record="centralised monitoring report; deviation listings; oversight / monitoring plan" party="sponsor; CRAs; site monitors and centralized monitoring">
          <ipd:source key="E6R3" loc="A1-3.11.4.5.4(b)(ii)" page="printed 34 / PDF 42"/>
          <ipd:source key="E6R3" loc="A1-3.11.4.2(a)" page="printed 31 / PDF 39"/>
          <ipd:source key="E6R3" loc="A1-3.11.4.2(b)" page="printed 31 / PDF 39"/>
          <ipd:source key="E8R1" loc="S6.1.3" page="printed 18"/>
          <ipd:source key="E8R1" loc="S3.3.2" page="printed 6"/>
          <ipd:source key="E6R3" loc="A1-3.11.3" page="printed 30 / PDF 38"/>
          <ipd:source key="E6R3" loc="A1-3.16.1(b)" page="printed 39 / PDF 47"/>
          <ipd:source key="E6R3" loc="A2-3.8" page="printed 62 / PDF 70"/>
          <ipd:source key="E6R3" loc="A1-3.11.4.5.4(c)" page="printed 34 / PDF 42"/>
          <ipd:source key="FDA-RBM13" loc="SIII.B" page="printed 8"/>
          <ipd:source key="FDA-PD24" loc="SIII.B.2" page="printed 6; lines 227-228; printed 9; lines 314-317"/>
          <ipd:source key="TCB-PD-TIRS" loc="SIdentify-and-Collect" page="journal pp. 733-742 (section page not confirmed; PMC HTML read)"/>
          <ipd:req id="REQ-037"/>
          <ipd:req id="REQ-036"/>
          <ipd:req id="REQ-035"/>
          <ipd:req id="REQ-038"/>
